1. What is the difference between AI and ML?
AI is the broader field of building systems that perform intelligent tasks. ML is a subset of AI in which systems learn patterns from data.

Q2. What is the difference between ML and deep learning?
ML includes many approaches, such as decision trees and linear regression. Deep learning is a subset of ML that uses multi-layer neural networks.

Q3. What is Generative AI?
Generative AI refers to systems that generate new content, such as text, images, audio or code, based on learned patterns and input prompts.

Q4. Is every AI system a deep-learning system?
No. Some AI systems use explicit rules, search or planning techniques without deep-learning models.

Q5. Is ChatGPT an example of Generative AI?
Yes. ChatGPT uses generative models to produce responses to user inputs.

